Z||000000||artherd||08-10-2001||07:07 AM||||Ok, so all I've got right now is the sig pic.<P>It's from the West Fest in SF where, <BR>thanks to the efforts of Geroge Miller <BR>and the rest of the guys at fieroshop, <BR>I was able not only to attend, but <BR>actually took second in Custom Coupe!<BR>more pics at <A HREF="http://www.cfog.org/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.cfog.org/</A> <P>Anyway, the car needs the 1.5" front and about 1" rear ride height lowering, though I'm impressed by how good the 17s look on the stock suspension.  When that's all done I plan a proper photo shoot on the coast, grin :)<P>How do I like them? Awesome. Totally awesome. It's like a new car. The ride is no harsher, infact it's smoother!  I recomend *any and all* fiero owners run right out and get a set of 17" wheels and grippy tyres.  All of you. Come on, do it :)<P>PS: Thanks to Trav(1FST2M6) for the wheels, hope your new ones look even more awesome on your 'Sweet Orange' GT!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
