Z||000006||artherd||08-10-2001||04:20 PM||||oops, they're Enkei Phanalex wheels, 17x7 40mm both front and rear (I'm looking for some 17x8 or ideally 17x9 of same, for rear <BR>wheels  :) (need to be around 55-60mm offset to fit the 9", but I'm going coilover soon I hope  :)<P>Need to get some more flattering shots. Hi Lisa yes they do look a lot like your wheels! (nice wheels by the way  :) similar 5/10spoke hybrid going on.<P>Trav, I think they looked even better on your orange car, but they are awesome in person on my formula ! :D)  Yes, they're really really really nice at speed, it's like I have twice the car as before, easially!<P>What amazed me most is that with 215/45 sidewalls, the ride around town, etc is actually smoother.  I was expecting to give up at least something in harshness for the whole new car the wheels made, but no! Better in EVERY way, yes!!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">   <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000007||FieroGTguy||08-10-2001||09:47 PM||||I have some 17" Konig wheels.  17x7 40mm offset.  Pics and info at <A HREF="http://www.fierostuff.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostuff.com</A> <P>Now for the kicker...  I will throw in the $50 shipping, $26 tuner lugs, and $12 hub rings, and the center caps for free.  <P>First to e-mail me an address to send the payment to gets them.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||1
